# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SOURDEN — Cloudflare redirects
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloudflare reads this file at deploy time from the static asset directory
# (`assets.directory` in wrangler.toml). Astro copies it from public/ into
# dist/ during the build. Syntax:
#   <from> <to> [status]
# Reference: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/redirects/
#
# The site builds with Astro `build.format: 'file'`, so every page ships as
# `<route>.html` and is served at the clean, slash-less URL documented in the
# spec (§33) — e.g. `/services/product-sourcing`. `html_handling` on the
# Worker handles that mapping; the rules below only tidy up legacy / alias
# URLs. Redirects are applied before assets are matched, so they win.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Canonicalise the root
/index.html          /                        301
/home                /                        301

# Sitemap alias — @astrojs/sitemap emits sitemap-index.xml
/sitemap.xml         /sitemap-index.xml       301

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RESERVED — when /products/ (spec §32) goes live, keep old category URLs
# pointing at the right place rather than letting them 404. Example:
#
# /products/hair-extensions/tape-in   /product-categories/tape-in-hair-extensions   301
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
